<title>JAPAN: Enix Corp jumps on software plans.</title>
<headline>Enix Corp jumps on software plans.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Enix Corp's shares rose on Friday, inspired by news that it had agreed with Sony Computer Entertainment to develop and sell software for Sony's PlayStation 32-bit game players, brokers said.</p>
<p>At 0508 GMT, the video game software maker's shares stood at 2,800 yen in over-the-counter trade, after finishing at 2,560 yen on Thursday.</p>
<p>It said in a statement on Thursday it will continue development and sales of software for Nintendo Co's game players, despite its new agreement woth Sony Computer.</p>
